# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# AW-018/AW-027/AW-028/PVL-018: the backdrop is a pose area, not a colour.
# deskicons.c held the rules for a Desktop nothing drew; these are the
# rules acting on icons that are actually there.
wait 12
note what it shows is the union of the Desktop folders, plus the Trash
expect-desk-icon notes.txt
expect-desk-icon .Trash
note its labels take their ink from the BACKDROP's brightness, so a dark
note backdrop gets white ones -- checked on the one icon no window covers
expect-pixel 520 58 ffffff
note a click on the backdrop is a click in a view
click 166 35
wait 3
expect-desk-selected-name notes.txt
note an icon is DRAGGED to where it should sit, and stays there
expect-icon-at photos 29 20
press 52 35
move 200 300
move 400 400
release 400 400
wait 6
expect-icon-at photos 377 385
note waited out, so the press that starts the next drag is not read as
note the second click of a double click on the icon just let go of
wait 40
note dragged against the Deskbar it comes back clear of it: the Desktop
note cannot scroll, so an icon behind the bar is an icon that is gone
press 400 400
move 700 200
move 850 150
release 850 150
wait 6
expect-icon-at photos 815 135
note and a double click opens the folder's own window
click 838 150
wait 2
click 838 150
wait 12
expect-windows 2
expect-title photos
quit
